            <ArticleTitle>Impending paradoxical embolism after coronary artery bypass grafting successful surgical treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of impending paradoxical embolism of a 22 cm long thromboembolus, straddling over a patent foramen ovale, detected by transthoracic and transesophageal echo 11 days after a coronary artery bypass operation. The patient underwent successful emergency removal of the clot and closure of the patent foramen ovale. A vena cava filter was placed because of new thrombi detected in deep veins of the legs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
